December gold fell $29.20 to $3,940.40 an ounce. Yesterday, the rate path was still just

00:01:45.851 --> 00:01:50.951
backdrop. Today, the Bank of Canada Governor and Senior Deputy Governor sit before the House of

00:01:50.951 --> 00:01:57.711
Commons Finance Committee, opening statement at 11 a.m. Eastern. Canada's S&amp;P Global Manufacturing

00:01:57.711 --> 00:02:04.791
Purchasing Managers Index, or PMI, printed 49.6 in October, the first contraction reading of

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:11.667
2026, with weaker output and new orders sitting behind those rate path questions. Cash secured

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:16.707
puts function as paid limit orders that compensate you for waiting to buy a stock you already want

00:02:16.707 --> 00:02:22.087
to own. It works like leaving a bid on a used car at a price you have already decided as fair,

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:27.787
and the dealer pays you a fee every month your offer stays live. If the car never comes down to your

00:02:27.787 --> 00:02:33.407
number, you keep the fee for waiting, and if it does, you buy at the price you named. In the options

00:02:33.407 --> 00:02:39.307
play growth lab example, a rank list of names shows the put strike, the premium collected, and the

00:02:39.307 --> 00:02:43.807
probability of assignment so you can compare the effective purchase price against your target

00:02:43.807 --> 00:02:49.527
entry, then filter that list by probability of profit and annualize return before placing the

00:02:49.527 --> 00:02:55.187
order. You open the position by selling the put and posting cash equal to the strike times 100

00:02:55.187 --> 00:03:00.787
shares. If the stock stays above the strike you keep the premium as income and repeat the process,

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:06.867
while assignment simply delivers the shares at your chosen net cost. Implementation starts in any

00:03:06.867 --> 00:03:12.467
options approved brokerage by scanning the chain for 30-45-day expires, where implied

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:17.267
volatility sits above the 20-day average, then confirming the premium covers at least

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:23.367
1% of the strike. Select a name trading near your target entry price, sell the 30-day put

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:28.427
at the strike one standard deviation below the current price, and record the premium received

00:03:28.427 --> 00:03:33.827
as a percentage of the strike. That single step turns waiting time into income while enforcing

00:03:33.827 --> 00:03:35.947
discipline on the entry you are willing to pay.

00:03:36.387 --> 00:03:43.487
The approach worked well in the 2022-2023 rate hike period, when elevated volatility-produced

00:03:43.487 --> 00:03:48.487
richer premiums, yet it fails when a sudden gap down leaves you assigned shares well below

00:03:48.487 --> 00:03:52.127
your original target, and forces an immediate unrealized loss.

00:03:52.827 --> 00:03:57.907
Canadian investors can run the same screen inside Questrade or Interactive Brokers, while

00:03:57.907 --> 00:04:03.447
While staying inside tax-free savings account, or TFSA, or registered retirement savings plan,

00:04:03.707 --> 00:04:09.167
or RRSP, contribution room, because the cash collateral counts toward the accounts settled

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:14.807
cash balance, and I have no financial relationship with options play, quest trade, interactive

00:04:14.807 --> 00:04:16.227
brokers, or wealth simple.

00:04:16.807 --> 00:04:19.887
Remember, if you already know your price, waiting can pay you.

00:04:20.755 --> 00:04:25.735
Open your brokerage tonight, pull the options chain for any stock you already own, calculate

00:04:25.735 --> 00:04:31.895
the 30-day cash secured put premium as a percentage of the strike, annualize that yield, and write down

00:04:31.895 --> 00:04:37.475
whether it exceeds your target cash return for the position. Palantir on the NASDAQ is the simulated

00:04:37.475 --> 00:04:43.395
weekly hold, a shares entry rather than the cash secured put screen, because the post earnings gap

00:04:43.395 --> 00:04:48.975
already cleared the level a put would have waited for. This is a simulated trade for learning purposes.

00:04:48.975 --> 00:04:54.975
1,000 dollars, five sessions from the next session's open, scored against the NASDAQ over

00:04:54.975 --> 00:04:57.835
that same window, with no discretionary exit.

00:04:58.495 --> 00:05:03.155
According to the Motley Fool, Palantir delivered another Blowout earnings report that included

00:05:03.155 --> 00:05:08.195
a first time ever milestone in commercial revenue trajectory, and that confirmed catalyst

00:05:08.195 --> 00:05:10.255
is the reason this name is on the ticket.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:16.080
The technical setup is a post-earnings gap holding above the 50 session average close with

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:22.160
volume confirmation, and nearest support sitting at the prior week's high, and 8% stop caps

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:28.720
the simulated loss at $80 on the $1,000 position if that level is reached intraday, and the target

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:33.500
is plus 3% to plus 7% over the 5-session window if momentum holds.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:39.340
In validation is a close below the 50-session average close on volume above the 20-session

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:44.480
average inside the hold window, that is the print that would prove the thesis wrong before

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:49.700
the stop has to do the work. Confidence is medium because the earnings catalyst is confirmed

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:55.100
and volume is supportive, yet sector rotation pressure on technology remains the uncertainty

00:05:55.100 --> 00:06:00.960
that keeps the rating off high. The rules-based record has shown negative average alpha in technology,

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:06.660
so that factor is not paying, and this holds still goes on because it is a clean test of whether a

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:12.380
confirmed earning surprise plus the volume filter and the 50-session filter can produce matched window

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:14.740
alpha inside a sector that has been a drag.

00:06:15.688 --> 00:06:21.168
Medium also borrows the calibration from the last closed bank hold, where a mix set up against

00:06:21.168 --> 00:06:25.828
rotation pressure was graded medium, and the stop was left to do its job rather than

00:06:25.828 --> 00:06:26.648
tightened on feel.

00:06:27.288 --> 00:06:33.548
We simulated buying Toronto Dominion on the TSX at the Wednesday open at $176 Canadian dollars

00:06:33.548 --> 00:06:39.848
in 80 cents, and exiting at the Tuesday close at $174 Canadian dollars in 75 cents.

00:06:39.848 --> 00:06:43.248
5 sessions, the 6% stop never touched.

00:06:43.688 --> 00:06:50.008
The position lost 1.16%, $11.60 on the $1,000 simulated ticket.

00:06:50.588 --> 00:06:57.608
While the NASDAQ lost 4.41% over the identical window, which is plus 3.25% of alpha.

00:06:58.268 --> 00:07:03.608
Stated confidence was medium, the valuation thesis was a Canadian bank trading below consensus

00:07:03.608 --> 00:07:09.988
its fair value, with stable U.S. operations contributing 35% to 40% of net income, and

00:07:09.988 --> 00:07:11.488
the invalidation never mattered.

00:07:12.168 --> 00:07:17.288
Medium fit the result, the absolute ticket went backwards and still beat the index, which

00:07:17.288 --> 00:07:20.108
is exactly the mixed tape that rating was meant to describe.

00:07:20.728 --> 00:07:26.208
A valuation edge produced positive alpha even when the dollar return was negative, and beating

00:07:26.208 --> 00:07:31.708
the NASDAQ by a little over 3 points on a losing trade, honestly, that feels pretty good.

00:07:31.708 --> 00:07:37.128
I would not adjust the stop, it held as designed, and the next test of that same discipline

00:07:37.128 --> 00:07:41.568
is whether an earning surprise name in a weak sector can do the same job without needing

00:07:41.568 --> 00:07:42.488
a rescue exit.

00:07:43.509 --> 00:07:47.989
Wealth simple lets you sell an entire fractional position and repurchase a whole share amount

00:07:47.989 --> 00:07:54.569
in one transaction inside a TFSA without triggering a contribution room issue, provided the net

00:07:54.569 --> 00:07:56.509
cash movement stays within the account.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:08:02.269
users access it in the app's trade ticket by selecting sell all, then entering the exact

00:08:02.269 --> 00:08:06.969
whole share quantity on the buy side, which is the cleanup step that keeps settled cash

00:08:06.969 --> 00:08:12.269
countable when you post collateral for a cash secured put. The Reddit discussion notes that

00:08:12.269 --> 00:08:17.409
some fractional amounts cannot be offset by buying the missing piece because of minimum trade sizes,

00:08:17.929 --> 00:08:22.529
making the sell and rebuy route the cleanest method for keeping every holding in whole shares.

00:08:22.529 --> 00:08:29.829
odd-lot leftovers complicated adjusted cost-base or ACB, tracking and superficial loss calculations

00:08:29.829 --> 00:08:34.989
when you rebalance, and this single ticket avoids a string of tiny trades that can draw attention

00:08:34.989 --> 00:08:40.249
under those rules while preserving the contribution room already used by the original purchase.

00:08:41.239 --> 00:08:47.659
The Commodity Futures Trading Commission, or CFTC, on Tuesday approved perpetual futures on individual

00:08:47.659 --> 00:08:52.899
